# DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)

When adding or changing code, **reuse or extract** instead of copying near-identical logic.

## Before duplicating

1. Search for an existing helper in `packages/{common,ui,db,types,validators}` or `modules/common/`.
2. If two+ call sites share the same algorithm, extract a named function/factory **in this change** (or the next incremental task if the extract is large).
3. Prefer **parameterized shared code** over parallel user/owner/web/dashboard copies.

## Where shared code lives

| Concern | Home |
| -------- | ---- |
| Cookies, API client, session factories, route helpers | `packages/common` |
| Reusable UI primitives / hooks without app routes | `packages/ui` |
| Repo helpers, table-parameterized deletes | `packages/db` |
| Domain enums/DTOs | `packages/types` |
| Nest boilerplate (cleanup cron shell, image upload) | `apps/api/src/modules/common` |
| App-only glue | thin wrapper in that app — keep `CLIENT_APP` / register path differences only |

## Do

```typescript
// ✅ one mapper, reused
export function toLegacyPaymentStatus(purchaseStatus: string, paymentStatus: string): PaymentStatus
status: toLegacyPaymentStatus(purchase.status, payment.status)
```

```typescript
// ✅ factory with app-specific config
createSessionService({ api, app: CLIENT_APP.WEB })
```

## Don't

```typescript
// ❌ copy the same ternary in use-case and mapper
purchase.status === CONFIRMED ? COMPLETED : payment.status === REJECTED ? …
```

```typescript
// ❌ redefine SESSION_STATUS in an app when `@repo/common` already exports it
```

## Exceptions (not DRY debt)

- Intentional product differences (web attendee landing vs dashboard organizer landing **content**).
- Generated files, migration history, thin re-exports.
- Tests that mirror production contracts on purpose.
- One-off adapters at system boundaries when abstraction would obscure the vendor/API.

## Scope discipline

- Do not DRY unrelated areas in the same PR.
- Large cross-app extracts (auth session stack, registration pipelines) are **incremental tasks** with a short plan — not a drive-by mega-refactor.
- Prefer clarity: extract when duplication causes drift risk; skip when the shared abstraction would be vaguer than two small copies.
